Appendix A. History: byte identity against a Solaris build of our own
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Before Sun's own shipped images became the reference, the GNU path was brought
to byte identity against a Sun-toolchain build of the pci configuration made on
the Solaris host (section 2). Those tests were the gate until sun-records
replaced them -- sun-records needs no capture and compares against images Sun
itself built, which is strictly stronger. The mixed-build facility they
introduced (REFERENCE_DIR) is still in obp-gnu.mk, and sun-records uses it for
the stamp.

They are kept because they are what actually found the defects, and because
the summary below is the only place the whole per-artefact comparison
against a Solaris build is written down.

