The tokenizer route that no longer exists
    Before the 32-bit engine, the GNU path tokenized with the 64-bit one, on
    two dictionaries Sun's build never makes (f64t32.dic and tokenize64.dic),
    generated once on Solaris and vendored as "seeds". Two measurements
    justified that route and are the reason it could be retired without
    re-proving anything downstream:
      - Every .tok in the tree tokenized twice on Solaris, with the shipped
        32-bit forth and with a 64-bit forth64: 42 of 42 FCode outputs
        identical, 128 B to 23,812 B, no exceptions. The engine's width does
        not reach the product.
      - The seeds regenerated on Linux against the Solaris pair: the .dic
        images differ as expected (engine-address class) while all 54
        products are identical.
    The seeds and their build target were deleted when bootstrap-dics.sh made
    them unnecessary.

Dropin list generation (didepend)
    builtin.fth identical (5,000 B). dropins.mk differs only in the path
    spelling and in one buildoptions line rewritten from dmake to GNU syntax;
    every dependency edge is the same.

Every tokenized dropin and every makedi record
    24 of 24 .fc and 27 of 27 non-bootprom .di identical -- after this exact
    comparison found two real build-layer defects:
      - dropins.src's `buildoptions vpci.fc:= FTHFLAGS += [define]
        64BIT-ASSIGNED?` passed through by didepend in dmake syntax and
        silently dropped by GNU make, with %.fc never passing -s
        "${FTHFLAGS}": vpci.fc was missing probe-reg.fth:405's
        assigned-addresses block, 24 functional bytes.
      - font.di was named gallant-romfont by an override of Sun's fonts.mk
        recipe, whose own name is `fonts` (17 bytes: the name and the header
        checksum).
    The hypothesis both defects had been blamed on -- "comp.c compiled by gcc
    compresses differently" -- was refuted in the process: every LZW payload
    is identical.

Mixed link: the GNU chain with the reference's own decomp.o
    reset.bin identical (3,964 B). Before openboot.ld pinned Sun ld's COMMON
    allocation order it differed in 70 bytes, all sethi/or immediates for
    decomp.o's six tentative symbols (input, tab_prefix, tab_suffix,
    data_count, output, de_stack), which the two linkers place in .bss in
    different orders; proven by relinking with --defsym at Sun's addresses,
    which made them identical. reset.o still differs in 2 bytes (5.3).
    reset.symbols, headers and acfheaders identical -- acfheaders only with
    LC_ALL=C sort, which is 1,138 B off under another locale's collation.

openboot.bin, record by record
    29 records; OBP and 27 dropins identical, bootprom differing (26,121
    bytes of an LZW-compressed record whose input differs by 181 bytes, 5.2).
    The first differing byte of the whole file is 3,972: that record's own
    size field.

decomp-size against the reference's object
    1314, matching Sun's own getsz.awk value for it.

